WEBVTT

1
00:02:08.614 --> 00:02:10.195
Wow.

2
00:02:12.195 --> 00:02:15.653
Well. you were right.
It's amazing.

3
00:02:17.864 --> 00:02:19.695
Was all that junk there
when you were little?

4
00:02:22.155 --> 00:02:24.863
No. Just the woods.

5
00:02:24.864 --> 00:02:28.279
Ah. so is that a thing
in the Finnish countryside?

6
00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.654
Just throw all your rubbish
in the woods?

7
00:02:30.655 --> 00:02:31.739
No.

8
00:02:33.655 --> 00:02:35.530
Well. maybe a little.

9
00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.946
-Aah!
-Oh. yes!

10
00:02:46.487 --> 00:02:47.986
I need to... I need to
carry you through.

11
00:02:47.987 --> 00:02:49.946
Yeah. Ohh!

12
00:02:51.197 --> 00:02:52.947
Aah! Ohh!

13
00:02:57.237 --> 00:02:58.405
Huh.

14
00:03:03.028 --> 00:03:04.112
Okay.

15
00:03:06.155 --> 00:03:07.612
This is. uh...

16
00:03:08.864 --> 00:03:09.989
Yeah.

17
00:03:10.778 --> 00:03:12.695
-Yes?
-Yeah.

18
00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:15.739
This is gonna be
a bit more work.

19
00:03:16.445 --> 00:03:18.320
And a bit of fixing.

20
00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:22.069
Patching up.
Put some carpet down there.

21
00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:23.319
Have plenty of time after work.

22
00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:26.739
I... wanna show you something.

23
00:03:29.195 --> 00:03:32.904
This used to be
my and Taru's bedroom

24
00:03:32.905 --> 00:03:35.987
when we spent the summers
here with Grandma.

25
00:03:37.697 --> 00:03:41.822
There was this...
lovely green wallpaper.

26
00:03:43.987 --> 00:03:45.736
It's still here!

27
00:03:45.737 --> 00:03:48.071
Oh. wow.

28
00:03:48.072 --> 00:03:49.529
Hmm.

29
00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:54.111
Well...

30
00:03:54.112 --> 00:03:56.447
we did want nature close by.

31
00:03:57.697 --> 00:04:00.072
-This is...
-We'll get rid of it.

32
00:04:00.739 --> 00:04:02.027
Look.

33
00:04:02.028 --> 00:04:05.779
There used to be
an armchair here

34
00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:08.489
for reading bedtime stories.

35
00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:12.069
And then a dollhouse over here.

36
00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:15.403
This lovely old rocking horse
over here.

37
00:04:15.489 --> 00:04:20.279
And then we can put
the crib for the baby here.

38
00:04:24.321 --> 00:04:26.070
There's definitely enough room.

39
00:04:26.071 --> 00:04:28.904
For all three kids.

40
00:04:30.571 --> 00:04:32.362
For all three kids.

41
00:04:39.737 --> 00:04:40.987
And...

42
00:04:42.572 --> 00:04:44.528
What about London?

43
00:04:44.529 --> 00:04:46.697
Fuck London.

44
00:04:50.237 --> 00:04:51.653
Hmm.

45
00:05:00.612 --> 00:05:02.321
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

46
00:05:07.654 --> 00:05:09.152
Whoa!

47
00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:23.986
Whoo!

48
00:06:25.029 --> 00:06:26.445
Saga?

49
00:07:05.154 --> 00:07:06.446
Jesus.

50
00:07:06.447 --> 00:07:07.822
Saga!

51
00:07:10.446 --> 00:07:12.611
Oh. my God!

52
00:07:15.528 --> 00:07:16.737
Listen.

53
00:07:24.696 --> 00:07:26.821
As you shout.
so will the forest answer.

54
00:07:28.487 --> 00:07:30.236
What?

55
00:07:30.237 --> 00:07:32.362
It's a saying in Finland.

56
00:07:33.322 --> 00:07:35.903
I used to sneak here in secret.

57
00:07:35.904 --> 00:07:37.278
Why?

58
00:07:37.279 --> 00:07:39.697
Grandma forbid me to come.

59
00:07:43.112 --> 00:07:45.111
The forest takes its own.

60
00:07:45.112 --> 00:07:47.612
Ohh. Really?

61
00:07:49.654 --> 00:07:51.447
Make me a mother.

62
00:08:47.779 --> 00:08:49.279
A lot of patching up.

63
00:08:50.154 --> 00:08:52.362
Is she all right?

64
00:08:52.363 --> 00:08:53.404
What is this?

65
00:08:56.322 --> 00:08:57.613
Is it alright?

66
00:08:59.863 --> 00:09:03.487
W-What's happening?
What is happening?

67
00:09:03.488 --> 00:09:05.279
What's the matter with it?

68
00:09:05.779 --> 00:09:07.113
What's happening?

69
00:09:08.739 --> 00:09:10.696
What's wrong with it?

70
00:09:12.321 --> 00:09:15.195
Shh.

71
00:09:43.447 --> 00:09:45.197
I was so worried.

72
00:09:53.279 --> 00:09:55.072
These are for you.

73
00:09:59.238 --> 00:10:00.864
Is he okay?

74
00:10:03.363 --> 00:10:06.863
Yeah. Yeah. He's. uh...

75
00:10:10.114 --> 00:10:11.777
You're both fine.

76
00:10:11.778 --> 00:10:13.571
I want to see him.

77
00:10:15.489 --> 00:10:16.696
Okay.

78
00:10:18.364 --> 00:10:21.029
Yeah. Wait.

79
00:10:28.239 --> 00:10:30.739
Bring him here.
I want to hold him.

80
00:10:41.572 --> 00:10:43.278
He won't break.

81
00:10:43.279 --> 00:10:45.237
Oh. yeah. I know.

82
00:10:45.238 --> 00:10:47.528
I can show you.

83
00:10:47.529 --> 00:10:49.403
You can hold him like this.

84
00:10:51.072 --> 00:10:53.153
And into Mommy's arms.

85
00:10:57.072 --> 00:10:58.862
-Scooch.
-Yeah.

86
00:10:58.863 --> 00:11:01.321
Daddy is like a support network
at this stage.

87
00:11:01.322 --> 00:11:03.862
Yeah...

88
00:11:11.028 --> 00:11:12.903
Mummy's hug calms down.

89
00:11:21.529 --> 00:11:24.071
Never seen such a hairy baby.

90
00:11:26.029 --> 00:11:27.404
Is this...

91
00:11:29.196 --> 00:11:31.489
You have a healthy baby boy.

92
00:11:39.029 --> 00:11:40.112
You had a pretty

93
00:11:40.113 --> 00:11:43.028
difficult birth. so you
can get therapy if...

94
00:11:43.029 --> 00:11:45.947
No. everything's all right.
I'm totally fine.

95
00:11:46.863 --> 00:11:48.446
What's that?

96
00:11:48.447 --> 00:11:51.446
Nothing.
Everything is good.

97
00:11:51.447 --> 00:11:53.362
-Okay.
-Okay.

98
00:11:53.363 --> 00:11:55.322
-Get the flowers.
-Oh.

99
00:11:56.613 --> 00:11:58.321
Yeah.

100
00:11:59.904 --> 00:12:01.988
Eh. Take another one.

101
00:12:12.903 --> 00:12:14.695
Wait. darling.
I can... I can help.

102
00:12:14.696 --> 00:12:16.779
No. no. I'm good.

103
00:12:46.113 --> 00:12:48.862
This is where it all begins.

104
00:12:48.863 --> 00:12:49.946
Us.

105
00:12:57.697 --> 00:12:59.653
Here we go.

106
00:13:01.822 --> 00:13:04.321
It's your new home.

107
00:13:04.322 --> 00:13:06.112
Look how Daddy's
renovated it all for you.

108
00:13:06.113 --> 00:13:09.402
-Jon. He's hungry.
-Upstairs.

109
00:13:09.403 --> 00:13:11.195
Down there's the kitchen.

110
00:13:12.696 --> 00:13:14.028
Oh. look at this.

111
00:13:15.739 --> 00:13:17.738
Big window.

112
00:13:17.739 --> 00:13:20.903
And this is
a very special room...

113
00:13:22.279 --> 00:13:24.320
Mummy's made just for you.

114
00:13:24.321 --> 00:13:25.820
With lots of love.

115
00:13:36.322 --> 00:13:37.987
-Yeah?
-Yeah.

116
00:13:37.988 --> 00:13:40.112
Shh.

117
00:13:40.113 --> 00:13:43.404
Mummy's little darling.
you'll get some food soon.

118
00:13:50.863 --> 00:13:51.863
Darling.

119
00:13:52.697 --> 00:13:53.697
Yes.

120
00:14:01.279 --> 00:14:02.322
There.

121
00:14:05.529 --> 00:14:07.321
Ow!

122
00:14:07.322 --> 00:14:09.153
Oh. Does it hurt?

123
00:14:09.239 --> 00:14:11.321
No. No. no.

124
00:14:13.571 --> 00:14:14.739
You okay?

125
00:14:15.821 --> 00:14:17.114
Yeah.

126
00:14:22.404 --> 00:14:24.238
Remember what the midwife said.

127
00:14:24.239 --> 00:14:26.029
Eye contact is crucial.

128
00:14:27.154 --> 00:14:28.320
Yeah.

129
00:14:34.822 --> 00:14:37.903
Maybe upholstery's a bit off.

130
00:14:37.904 --> 00:14:40.028
Let me just get this up.

131
00:14:40.029 --> 00:14:42.487
I... I know how to do this.

132
00:14:45.488 --> 00:14:47.903
Is the nipple hitting
the roof of the mouth?

133
00:14:47.904 --> 00:14:49.028
Just...

134
00:14:49.029 --> 00:14:50.447
Stop it!

135
00:14:51.572 --> 00:14:53.072
It's... Sorry.

136
00:15:01.364 --> 00:15:04.322
Mummy's sweetheart. hi!

137
00:15:16.489 --> 00:15:18.363
Careful! He could fall!

138
00:15:18.364 --> 00:15:20.570
It hurts me when I touch.

139
00:15:20.571 --> 00:15:23.945
I'm your daddy. We're not
gonna hurt you. are we?

140
00:15:23.946 --> 00:15:25.821
That's it.

141
00:15:26.946 --> 00:15:28.903
There we go. That's better.

142
00:15:28.904 --> 00:15:31.321
It's like a tiny
little tail sprout.

143
00:15:32.697 --> 00:15:34.362
That's cute.

144
00:15:38.904 --> 00:15:40.238
Better?

145
00:16:35.238 --> 00:16:39.153
Good evening. good night.

146
00:16:39.154 --> 00:16:43.362
With roses adorned.

147
00:16:43.363 --> 00:16:47.153
With carnations covered.

148
00:16:47.154 --> 00:16:51.321
Slip under the covers

149
00:16:51.322 --> 00:16:54.987
Early tomorrow. so God willing.

150
00:16:54.988 --> 00:16:59.196
You will wake once again

151
00:16:59.197 --> 00:17:03.152
Early tomorrow...

152
00:17:03.153 --> 00:17:06.403
What... What if
you stop singing?

153
00:17:06.404 --> 00:17:07.945
I'm doing my best.

154
00:17:07.946 --> 00:17:10.528
I know.
I'm... I'm just trying to help.

155
00:17:10.614 --> 00:17:13.569
Yeah. but he doesn't
want to sleep.

156
00:17:13.570 --> 00:17:16.945
No. he just doesn't
wanna sleep alone. do ya?

157
00:17:19.904 --> 00:17:22.239
That's better now. isn't it?

158
00:17:24.739 --> 00:17:26.779
He's lifting his head up.

159
00:17:27.445 --> 00:17:30.444
How's he doing that?

160
00:17:30.445 --> 00:17:33.279
Oh. you're such a little
miracle. Christian. aren't you?

161
00:17:35.571 --> 00:17:39.404
Does he look like
a Christian to you?

162
00:18:39.696 --> 00:18:42.445
Saga.

163
00:18:42.446 --> 00:18:46.238
Just put him
into those party clothes now!

164
00:18:49.071 --> 00:18:50.446
So nice that you came.

165
00:18:58.779 --> 00:19:00.696
Saga?

166
00:19:01.864 --> 00:19:03.488
So nice that you came.

167
00:19:08.489 --> 00:19:10.153
-Mother.
-Surprise!

168
00:19:11.114 --> 00:19:13.153
-We came to help you.
-Hi!

169
00:19:13.239 --> 00:19:16.444
We couldn't wait
to see the little prince!

170
00:19:16.445 --> 00:19:18.404
-And a lovely dress!
-Thank you.

171
00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:21.153
You look really tired.

172
00:19:21.154 --> 00:19:22.863
I'm fine.

173
00:19:22.864 --> 00:19:24.320
Your button is undone.

174
00:19:26.404 --> 00:19:27.570
It's okay.

175
00:19:28.404 --> 00:19:31.989
It's still a bit unfinished
as the baby was born early.

176
00:19:32.863 --> 00:19:34.446
there wasn't time.

177
00:19:35.529 --> 00:19:39.446
But when it's all done.
the view out will be beautiful.

178
00:19:40.696 --> 00:19:44.946
Was it necessary to do all this
with you so exhausted?

179
00:19:46.446 --> 00:19:49.113
Hey. it's really beautiful.

180
00:19:52.029 --> 00:19:54.820
-Wow!
-Look. Anna!

181
00:19:54.821 --> 00:19:58.279
What a dream room
Auntie has made!

182
00:19:59.196 --> 00:20:01.321
-Isn't it fine?
-Yes!

183
00:20:02.988 --> 00:20:06.488
-Isn't this wallpaper...
-Just like when we were kids.

184
00:20:07.863 --> 00:20:08.863
It's lovely.

185
00:20:08.989 --> 00:20:10.945
When will you go back to work?

186
00:20:11.364 --> 00:20:12.653
Uh...

187
00:20:14.489 --> 00:20:15.903
I'm taking five years off.

188
00:20:15.989 --> 00:20:17.988
-What?
-Yeah.

189
00:20:17.989 --> 00:20:19.944
We'll have two more babies.

190
00:20:19.945 --> 00:20:23.363
Kids are small
for such a short time.

191
00:20:23.364 --> 00:20:25.445
If you miss
all those lovely moments.

192
00:20:26.404 --> 00:20:27.778
you can't get them back.

193
00:20:27.779 --> 00:20:28.779
Yes. but...

194
00:20:31.864 --> 00:20:34.320
Yeah. he's not very happy
at the moment.

195
00:20:34.321 --> 00:20:36.070
I have a sleeve.
Should we try?

196
00:20:36.071 --> 00:20:37.071
Oh. yeah.

197
00:20:37.529 --> 00:20:40.196
-Clothes hurt him.
-You little darling!

198
00:20:40.738 --> 00:20:43.903
Come here now.
You're a big boy!

199
00:20:43.904 --> 00:20:45.695
Let's give you to your grandma.

200
00:20:45.696 --> 00:20:47.363
Careful. he's a bit heavy.

201
00:20:48.029 --> 00:20:50.195
-Who do we have here...
-I can take it...

202
00:20:50.196 --> 00:20:51.863
I didn't kill you two either.

203
00:20:52.738 --> 00:20:55.321
Sounds like he's hungry.
Has he eaten?

204
00:20:55.946 --> 00:20:57.321
Yes. he's eaten.

205
00:20:57.988 --> 00:20:59.445
Why on Earth did you want

206
00:20:59.446 --> 00:21:00.988
to move in to this wilderness?

207
00:21:00.989 --> 00:21:02.902
I got it wrong.

208
00:21:02.903 --> 00:21:05.778
Oh. We just... We just wanted
him to grow up around nature.

209
00:21:05.779 --> 00:21:09.903
I know that Saga always liked
more trees than people.

210
00:21:09.989 --> 00:21:11.319
What do you mean?

211
00:21:11.320 --> 00:21:12.819
What was that?

212
00:21:12.820 --> 00:21:14.569
No. Saga was a bit
antisocial as a kid.

213
00:21:14.570 --> 00:21:16.319
You always said

214
00:21:16.320 --> 00:21:20.070
your friends laughed at you
for being so weird.

215
00:21:23.114 --> 00:21:24.114
Let go!

216
00:21:24.904 --> 00:21:26.153
Ohh!

217
00:21:28.570 --> 00:21:30.154
Mother! Help!

218
00:21:31.404 --> 00:21:32.528
I'll call an ambulance.

219
00:21:32.529 --> 00:21:34.113
Get my doctor's bag.

220
00:21:40.446 --> 00:21:41.446
Are you okay?

221
00:21:44.029 --> 00:21:46.862
I don't know how it could
yank so hard.

222
00:21:46.863 --> 00:21:50.238
-I wasn't holding him wrong.
-I didn't mean that.

223
00:21:51.988 --> 00:21:55.904
I've been wondering if there's
something wrong with it.

224
00:21:56.488 --> 00:21:58.653
I don't think
babies should be like that.

225
00:21:58.654 --> 00:22:00.529
You were just like that
as a baby.

226
00:22:04.029 --> 00:22:06.987
-Are you staying the night?
-Overnight flight to Boston.

227
00:22:06.988 --> 00:22:08.070
The lectures begin.

228
00:22:09.070 --> 00:22:10.778
Weren't you supposed
to be retired?

229
00:22:11.195 --> 00:22:14.403
I just don't happen to be
a bun-baking granny

230
00:22:14.489 --> 00:22:17.445
sacrificing all their time
to grandchildren.

231
00:22:20.529 --> 00:22:22.529
So you didn't get that
from Grandma.

232
00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:27.864
You have a really romanticised
idea of how people should be.

233
00:22:29.445 --> 00:22:32.362
Hi! So nice that you came!

234
00:22:32.363 --> 00:22:34.488
-Congratulations!
-Thank you!

235
00:22:35.613 --> 00:22:37.987
-Are you okay?
-Yeah. I am.

236
00:22:37.988 --> 00:22:39.988
Congratulations!

237
00:22:43.196 --> 00:22:45.237
Gets a bit lost. but...

238
00:22:46.571 --> 00:22:47.696
There he is!

239
00:22:47.946 --> 00:22:50.321
He's a bit of
a crybaby now but...

240
00:22:54.529 --> 00:22:56.903
-Strong lungs. at least!
-That's right.

241
00:22:56.904 --> 00:22:59.320
Loud enough. Congratulations!

242
00:22:59.321 --> 00:23:00.614
Mum. Let's go.

243
00:23:01.739 --> 00:23:02.737
Yeah.

244
00:23:02.738 --> 00:23:06.403
I'll calm him down a bit here.
But so lovely that you came.

245
00:23:06.404 --> 00:23:07.696
See you in a minute!

246
00:23:11.614 --> 00:23:13.569
Why did it look so weird?

247
00:23:13.570 --> 00:23:14.903
Shh!

248
00:23:28.989 --> 00:23:31.653
No. I'm. uh.
director of sustainability.

249
00:23:35.738 --> 00:23:37.737
Get me an earlier ticket.

250
00:23:37.738 --> 00:23:40.153
No. No. no. no. For tonight.

251
00:23:40.154 --> 00:23:41.570
Yes. yes. Tonight.

252
00:23:41.571 --> 00:23:44.363
-Babies are usually cute.
-Yeah.

253
00:23:47.404 --> 00:23:49.238
She chose the dress herself.

254
00:24:00.404 --> 00:24:02.237
Shh. shh. shh. shh.

255
00:24:02.238 --> 00:24:05.028
Shh. shh. shh. shh. shh.

256
00:24:22.779 --> 00:24:24.363
I can take Christian.

257
00:24:24.364 --> 00:24:26.528
He wants to be in the dark.

258
00:24:26.529 --> 00:24:27.820
Well...

259
00:24:29.029 --> 00:24:30.864
He's kind of why
they're all here.

260
00:24:32.488 --> 00:24:33.570
Ohh.

261
00:24:34.696 --> 00:24:36.071
Yeah.

262
00:24:41.238 --> 00:24:45.028
Dear friends.
Thank you all for coming.

263
00:24:45.029 --> 00:24:47.195
Most of you have been
absolutely lovely.

264
00:24:47.196 --> 00:24:49.320
Others. a little bit Finnish.

265
00:24:49.321 --> 00:24:51.195
In a good way.

266
00:24:51.196 --> 00:24:52.778
Unfortunately. my father.
due to illness.

267
00:24:52.779 --> 00:24:55.403
he can't make it
and bless our child.

268
00:24:57.113 --> 00:24:59.403
But he will be
very pleased to hear

269
00:24:59.404 --> 00:25:02.487
that our baby's name is...

270
00:25:06.446 --> 00:25:07.738
Kuura.

271
00:25:08.739 --> 00:25:09.739
What?

272
00:25:12.364 --> 00:25:13.903
His name is Kuura.

273
00:25:46.529 --> 00:25:50.113
I just felt a little sick. But
so lovely that you came!

274
00:25:50.863 --> 00:25:51.863
Bye!

275
00:25:53.821 --> 00:25:56.696
Now first of all.
you take care of yourself.

276
00:25:57.363 --> 00:25:58.863
That's the most important thing.

277
00:26:00.904 --> 00:26:02.363
You should know.

278
00:26:05.238 --> 00:26:06.238
Bye!

279
00:26:23.279 --> 00:26:25.154
You're mad at me.

280
00:26:27.279 --> 00:26:30.864
I think Kuura is a...
beautiful name.

281
00:26:32.904 --> 00:26:36.320
But we have to
do this together. okay?

282
00:26:36.321 --> 00:26:38.070
We have to be us...

283
00:26:38.071 --> 00:26:40.029
or none of this makes sense.

284
00:26:41.738 --> 00:26:44.612
It makes me feel bad
when you just decide something

285
00:26:44.613 --> 00:26:47.029
and then ride right over me.

286
00:26:47.946 --> 00:26:51.153
I do everything wrong
all the time.

287
00:26:51.154 --> 00:26:53.403
That's not what I'm saying.

288
00:26:53.404 --> 00:26:56.987
Why are you correcting
every single thing I do?

289
00:26:56.988 --> 00:26:58.862
I can't do anything right.

290
00:26:58.863 --> 00:27:01.321
You made us a beautiful baby.

291
00:27:04.363 --> 00:27:07.445
I'm just... trying to help.

292
00:27:07.446 --> 00:27:09.695
Then stop instructing me...

293
00:27:11.028 --> 00:27:14.403
telling me to do this
and not to do that.

294
00:27:14.489 --> 00:27:18.195
You could just...
praise me sometimes.

295
00:27:21.739 --> 00:27:24.114
And I am sorry about the name.

296
00:27:31.654 --> 00:27:33.195
Hey.

297
00:27:37.696 --> 00:27:40.362
Why don't you want
to kiss me anymore?

298
00:27:40.363 --> 00:27:43.362
What? I do. All the time.

299
00:27:43.363 --> 00:27:44.654
But you don't.

300
00:27:46.363 --> 00:27:47.945
Okay.

301
00:27:47.946 --> 00:27:51.862
This is all new and weird
for both of us.

302
00:27:56.321 --> 00:27:59.112
But you are the best mum
in the world.

303
00:28:02.071 --> 00:28:03.987
There's something wrong with it.

304
00:28:03.988 --> 00:28:06.903
"Him." You mean "him."

305
00:28:06.904 --> 00:28:09.653
He's just a bit sensitive
to sunlight.

306
00:28:09.739 --> 00:28:11.363
He'll be fine.

307
00:28:20.864 --> 00:28:21.904
Saga!

308
00:28:23.114 --> 00:28:24.114
Hey!

309
00:28:24.654 --> 00:28:25.778
Shh!

310
00:28:25.779 --> 00:28:27.114
What are you doing?

311
00:28:29.320 --> 00:28:32.195
Hey. you mustn't
rattle him like that!

312
00:28:32.196 --> 00:28:33.695
Shh! Shh. shh. shh. shh!

313
00:28:35.363 --> 00:28:36.446
Now it sleeps.

314
00:28:36.904 --> 00:28:38.696
It doesn't sleep at all
at nights.

315
00:28:39.779 --> 00:28:40.779
Hi!

316
00:28:44.196 --> 00:28:45.404
-Look.
-Yeah.

317
00:28:48.029 --> 00:28:50.238
You can move around
much better already.

318
00:28:50.863 --> 00:28:52.320
What did the doctors say?

319
00:28:52.321 --> 00:28:54.528
They said I am fully healed.

320
00:28:54.529 --> 00:28:55.738
That's lovely!

321
00:28:57.404 --> 00:28:58.404
Isn't it?

322
00:28:59.488 --> 00:29:00.945
I'm still pig ugly.

323
00:29:00.946 --> 00:29:04.029
Hey. nonsense!
Why do you say that for?

324
00:29:05.154 --> 00:29:07.446
Everything is really
fine now. right?

325
00:29:11.153 --> 00:29:12.153
Yeah.

326
00:29:13.903 --> 00:29:16.320
Who's awake now?

327
00:29:18.404 --> 00:29:21.363
Will you smile for Auntie?

328
00:29:21.364 --> 00:29:24.363
-It never smiles.
-Good!

329
00:29:24.364 --> 00:29:25.779
It's a bit strange.

330
00:29:30.739 --> 00:29:31.739
Hey. darling!

331
00:29:32.154 --> 00:29:35.821
Look. he's smiling. Yes!

332
00:29:37.071 --> 00:29:38.862
-Good.
-That's just a grimace.

333
00:29:38.863 --> 00:29:42.820
It isn't! Look at it! Good!

334
00:29:42.821 --> 00:29:43.821
I'm looking.

335
00:29:50.404 --> 00:29:51.571
What was that?

336
00:29:54.488 --> 00:29:55.988
Hey. Anna!

337
00:30:01.946 --> 00:30:04.820
Ugh. It's so awful.

338
00:30:04.821 --> 00:30:07.737
Yeah. I'm just trying to...
Just making a pile over here.

339
00:30:07.738 --> 00:30:09.569
Okay.

340
00:30:09.570 --> 00:30:11.902
Did I ever tell you
what Granny said

341
00:30:11.903 --> 00:30:13.819
right towards the end?

342
00:30:13.820 --> 00:30:18.278
She called me. went on and on
about all this junk.

343
00:30:18.279 --> 00:30:22.569
saying it kept "them" away
or something.

344
00:30:22.570 --> 00:30:24.613
Keeps out the neighbors?

345
00:30:24.614 --> 00:30:26.613
How very Finnish.

346
00:30:26.614 --> 00:30:32.862
No. Cold iron.
"Cold iron burns them."

347
00:30:32.863 --> 00:30:35.862
She lived in a world of her own.
Poor thing.

348
00:30:59.738 --> 00:31:01.029
Don't.

349
00:31:03.153 --> 00:31:04.988
Are you still in pain?

350
00:31:09.239 --> 00:31:11.364
Is it asleep?

351
00:31:14.989 --> 00:31:17.239
Please call him "him."

352
00:31:21.114 --> 00:31:24.069
We don't have to do anything.

353
00:31:24.070 --> 00:31:25.614
Just thought I'd be nice.

354
00:31:26.614 --> 00:31:28.739
Or nasty.

355
00:31:33.571 --> 00:31:35.571
You're beautiful.

356
00:31:51.279 --> 00:31:52.946
I love you.

357
00:32:10.070 --> 00:32:12.364
Look! It's sitting!

358
00:32:15.864 --> 00:32:18.570
No. Come on.
Babies can't sit at that age.

359
00:32:24.739 --> 00:32:26.114
Oh. yeah.

360
00:32:28.654 --> 00:32:30.194
Stop it!

361
00:32:37.238 --> 00:32:39.820
Sorry. I just...

362
00:32:39.821 --> 00:32:42.821
You need rest.
So go to sleep.

363
00:32:44.404 --> 00:32:45.653
Leave him. I don't mind.

364
00:32:45.654 --> 00:32:47.488
I'll handle it.

365
00:32:58.488 --> 00:33:00.239
Shh. shh.

366
00:33:31.320 --> 00:33:33.279
MUM

367
00:34:02.821 --> 00:34:05.029
Well. hi!

368
00:34:06.113 --> 00:34:07.821
Finally you answered.

369
00:34:09.778 --> 00:34:10.778
Saga!

370
00:34:13.528 --> 00:34:14.569
Oh. hi.

371
00:34:14.570 --> 00:34:16.320
I forgot it's night there.

372
00:34:17.155 --> 00:34:19.070
Isn't Kuura sleeping yet?

373
00:34:21.364 --> 00:34:22.364
Well.

374
00:34:23.155 --> 00:34:25.945
You were a night owl like him
when you were little.

375
00:34:26.695 --> 00:34:28.279
You had something to say?

376
00:34:28.280 --> 00:34:29.654
I had?

377
00:34:29.655 --> 00:34:31.364
Yes. you tried to call.

378
00:34:34.322 --> 00:34:35.322
Saga!

379
00:34:35.780 --> 00:34:36.780
Um...

380
00:34:37.655 --> 00:34:40.821
Did Grandma ever say anything
about this forest?

381
00:34:40.822 --> 00:34:41.862
The forest?

382
00:34:43.405 --> 00:34:47.071
She always said there's
something dangerous in it.

383
00:34:47.072 --> 00:34:49.612
That's one of her stories.

384
00:34:50.405 --> 00:34:54.486
She believed
there were some... whatever.

385
00:35:01.030 --> 00:35:02.030
Saga?

386
00:35:03.028 --> 00:35:04.780
You been able to sleep at all?

387
00:35:10.028 --> 00:35:13.903
Let Jon put Kuura to bed
for a change.

388
00:35:16.780 --> 00:35:18.405
You must get some sleep.

389
00:35:18.905 --> 00:35:20.405
Yeah. everything is fine.

390
00:35:21.239 --> 00:35:22.529
Saga!

391
00:35:57.947 --> 00:36:00.780
Saga? Saga?

392
00:36:08.114 --> 00:36:09.903
What have you done?

393
00:36:19.070 --> 00:36:20.529
There was...

394
00:36:20.530 --> 00:36:22.319
What?

395
00:36:22.320 --> 00:36:24.613
The floor. It was rotten and...

396
00:36:24.614 --> 00:36:27.364
How has that tree grown back?

397
00:36:30.445 --> 00:36:34.322
Kuura. He was calling it.

398
00:36:36.155 --> 00:36:37.572
Okay.

399
00:36:39.155 --> 00:36:41.111
I think that's something
we can talk with

400
00:36:41.112 --> 00:36:43.279
the child-health clinic about.

401
00:36:43.280 --> 00:36:45.279
I just want to know
what this is.

402
00:36:45.280 --> 00:36:48.280
Exactly. We'll get some help.

403
00:36:53.737 --> 00:36:56.822
Go ahead. I'll be fine.

404
00:38:13.653 --> 00:38:16.570
How briskly
you wave your arms about!

405
00:38:17.570 --> 00:38:21.280
You're such a tall
and heavy boy.

406
00:38:32.947 --> 00:38:35.111
Your boy is perfectly healthy.

407
00:38:35.112 --> 00:38:38.529
Sorry. Uh. like I said
before. my Finnish...

408
00:38:38.530 --> 00:38:40.236
I'm sorry.

409
00:38:40.237 --> 00:38:42.236
Shouldn't you examine this?

410
00:38:42.237 --> 00:38:44.780
You can put his clothes on now.

411
00:38:46.655 --> 00:38:48.029
I can dress him.

412
00:38:48.030 --> 00:38:50.322
No. He's quiet now.

413
00:38:51.905 --> 00:38:53.572
Don't touch him.

414
00:38:55.697 --> 00:38:57.946
It'll scream
the moment you try to dress it.

415
00:38:57.947 --> 00:39:00.155
He may have
some sensory defensiveness.

416
00:39:01.155 --> 00:39:02.611
And perhaps a bit...

417
00:39:05.030 --> 00:39:07.821
Yes. Each baby is different.

418
00:39:07.822 --> 00:39:10.403
He is exceptionally
well developed

419
00:39:10.489 --> 00:39:12.653
and really big for his age!

420
00:39:12.989 --> 00:39:14.153
Good. strong muscles.

421
00:39:14.239 --> 00:39:16.738
Like an ape.

422
00:39:16.739 --> 00:39:19.488
Yeah. when he was born.
he had hair all over him.

423
00:39:19.489 --> 00:39:21.404
That's quite normal.

424
00:39:21.405 --> 00:39:23.319
But. um...

425
00:39:23.320 --> 00:39:25.654
He sucked my blood.

426
00:39:25.655 --> 00:39:27.363
It could be he's so hungry.

427
00:39:27.364 --> 00:39:30.029
he sucks whatever
he can get into his mouth.

428
00:39:30.030 --> 00:39:32.111
Well. you can tell
when he's hungry

429
00:39:32.112 --> 00:39:34.404
if you watch his face closely.

430
00:39:34.405 --> 00:39:37.486
You have probably
seen those little...

431
00:39:37.487 --> 00:39:39.321
sucking lip movements.

432
00:39:39.322 --> 00:39:41.154
And that's when
you can start feeding.

433
00:39:41.155 --> 00:39:43.779
Right. Okay. Yeah.

434
00:39:43.780 --> 00:39:46.404
You've been under pressure?

435
00:39:46.405 --> 00:39:48.361
No. I'm alright.

436
00:39:48.362 --> 00:39:52.736
But that's not the issue.
The problem is this baby.

437
00:39:52.737 --> 00:39:56.486
Or how you feel about him.

438
00:39:56.487 --> 00:40:01.321
All these difficult emotions
are perfectly normal.

439
00:40:01.322 --> 00:40:05.361
But the fact is. the baby feels
better when you feel better.

440
00:40:05.362 --> 00:40:08.319
I could make
a referral for you. Saga.

441
00:40:08.320 --> 00:40:10.777
And you can make an appointment
to talk about things.

442
00:40:10.778 --> 00:40:11.820
Thank you.

443
00:40:12.695 --> 00:40:14.694
And the father is alright?

444
00:40:14.695 --> 00:40:18.069
Yeah. Um. well. I mean...

445
00:40:18.070 --> 00:40:20.029
Sometimes the early days
with a small baby

446
00:40:20.030 --> 00:40:24.069
can be surprisingly hard.
especially for the mother.

447
00:40:24.070 --> 00:40:25.319
No. I understand that.

448
00:40:25.320 --> 00:40:27.319
For a lot of moms.

449
00:40:27.320 --> 00:40:30.905
this new creature
can feel completely alien.

450
00:40:51.780 --> 00:40:53.362
That went well. I guess.

451
00:40:55.697 --> 00:40:58.072
I won't breastfeed him anymore.

452
00:40:59.697 --> 00:41:02.197
-You mean... Wait.
-Never again.

453
00:41:03.653 --> 00:41:05.154
If you're struggling
to bond with Kuura...

454
00:41:05.155 --> 00:41:06.986
He sucks me dry.

455
00:41:06.987 --> 00:41:09.027
That's why breastfeeding
is so important for you!

456
00:41:09.028 --> 00:41:11.652
You're not even listening!

457
00:41:11.653 --> 00:41:13.527
Babe. I am.

458
00:41:15.114 --> 00:41:17.404
I am. okay?
I'm just trying to s...

459
00:41:17.405 --> 00:41:19.238
-I want...
-To sa...

460
00:41:19.239 --> 00:41:20.864
-I understand.
-you to stop!

461
00:41:22.864 --> 00:41:25.819
You're completely exhausted.
I get it.

462
00:41:25.820 --> 00:41:27.404
Your problem is...

463
00:41:27.405 --> 00:41:28.654
That child!

464
00:41:28.655 --> 00:41:30.613
No.

465
00:41:30.614 --> 00:41:33.696
Your problem is your
relationship with our child.

466
00:41:33.697 --> 00:41:34.986
What you're feeling is...

467
00:41:34.987 --> 00:41:37.905
Don't tell me how I feel!

468
00:41:45.947 --> 00:41:47.404
Of course they're early.

469
00:41:47.405 --> 00:41:48.779
Who?

470
00:41:48.780 --> 00:41:52.821
My parents.
We talked about this.

471
00:41:52.822 --> 00:41:54.155
When?

472
00:42:03.612 --> 00:42:05.529
Hey! Hello.

473
00:42:05.530 --> 00:42:08.402
It's so lovely to see you!

474
00:42:08.403 --> 00:42:09.944
Oh. is this the baby?

475
00:42:09.945 --> 00:42:11.403
Oh. yeah. he's just sleeping...

476
00:42:11.489 --> 00:42:13.070
-Oh.
-Son.

477
00:42:14.614 --> 00:42:15.820
Dad.

478
00:42:22.864 --> 00:42:26.069
Ooh. Hello...

479
00:42:26.070 --> 00:42:28.488
Ooh! Steady. love!

480
00:42:28.489 --> 00:42:30.069
Let's get some light on.
shall we?

481
00:42:30.070 --> 00:42:32.111
He's a bit sensitive to light.

482
00:42:32.112 --> 00:42:34.361
It's the child that ought to
learn from you. you know.

483
00:42:34.362 --> 00:42:36.405
Just let people
raise their own children.

484
00:42:36.530 --> 00:42:37.779
Oh!

485
00:42:37.780 --> 00:42:39.654
So lovely to see you. Saga.

486
00:42:39.655 --> 00:42:41.654
Welcome.

487
00:42:41.655 --> 00:42:43.361
I'm so sorry about this mess.

488
00:42:43.362 --> 00:42:46.029
The baby came early. and
we haven't found the time to...

489
00:42:46.030 --> 00:42:47.611
Oh. never you mind.

490
00:42:47.612 --> 00:42:49.154
Christian. shall
we give them the. um...

491
00:42:49.155 --> 00:42:51.029
-Oh. yes. yeah.
-For the housewarming.

492
00:42:51.030 --> 00:42:52.654
Ooh.

493
00:42:52.655 --> 00:42:53.904
Ta-da!

494
00:42:53.905 --> 00:42:56.236
-Wow.
-Wow.

495
00:42:56.237 --> 00:42:58.236
Made him myself.

496
00:42:58.237 --> 00:42:59.861
Yeah.

497
00:42:59.862 --> 00:43:01.364
Thank you.

498
00:43:02.862 --> 00:43:06.822
Right. well. uh. shall we
finally bless the child?

499
00:43:08.489 --> 00:43:09.778
I'll go and get him. then.

500
00:43:09.864 --> 00:43:11.278
Yes. please.

501
00:43:12.489 --> 00:43:15.402
I read that local tales here say

502
00:43:15.403 --> 00:43:18.238
that if you don't bless a child.
the trolls will take them.

503
00:43:18.239 --> 00:43:20.863
-Ohh.
-Do people still believe that?

504
00:43:20.864 --> 00:43:22.863
-No. Not anymore.
-That's why some families

505
00:43:22.864 --> 00:43:25.863
still have troll blood
running through their veins.

506
00:43:28.614 --> 00:43:31.944
Oh. Here's the little darling.

507
00:43:31.945 --> 00:43:35.571
Lucky for you. those old trolls
are afraid of holy water.

508
00:43:35.572 --> 00:43:38.280
So we can still save you.

509
00:43:42.987 --> 00:43:48.446
Sanctify this water by the
power of the Holy Spirit...

510
00:43:48.447 --> 00:43:52.361
so that they may be cleansed
and born again.

511
00:43:52.362 --> 00:43:54.821
Now. what happened
with the name?

512
00:43:54.822 --> 00:43:56.571
Oh. we...

513
00:43:56.572 --> 00:43:58.321
Your father took it pretty hard.

514
00:43:58.322 --> 00:44:00.113
Not that he'll say a word. mind.

515
00:44:00.114 --> 00:44:03.152
Almighty God. Heavenly Father.

516
00:44:03.153 --> 00:44:08.569
we ask you to bless this child
in the name of Jesus Christ.

517
00:44:16.320 --> 00:44:19.529
In the name of the Father...

518
00:44:19.530 --> 00:44:22.779
and of the Son...

519
00:44:22.780 --> 00:44:25.114
and of the Holy Spirit.

520
00:44:30.989 --> 00:44:33.072
-Amen.
-Amen.

521
00:44:35.612 --> 00:44:37.030
Amen.

522
00:44:46.612 --> 00:44:49.446
Ooh.

523
00:44:49.447 --> 00:44:51.947
Yeah. That's better.

524
00:44:54.112 --> 00:44:55.486
Is that...?

525
00:44:55.487 --> 00:44:56.986
Yeah. yeah.
The seeds you gave me.

526
00:44:56.987 --> 00:44:58.821
-Ohh!
-They're taking really well.

527
00:44:58.822 --> 00:45:01.738
You've got some pumpkin
growing and some courgette.

528
00:45:01.739 --> 00:45:03.402
Yeah.
And some beetroot here.

529
00:45:03.403 --> 00:45:06.236
-And kale.
-And is the soil good?

530
00:45:06.237 --> 00:45:09.569
Yeah. It's taken
a bit of work. but it's...

531
00:45:09.570 --> 00:45:12.903
Well. it's certainly
all looking beautiful.

532
00:45:14.945 --> 00:45:16.779
How did this get here?

533
00:45:16.780 --> 00:45:19.194
Are you alright. dear?

534
00:45:19.195 --> 00:45:21.989
Yes. This just... grew.

535
00:45:24.114 --> 00:45:25.655
Makes no sense.

536
00:45:26.739 --> 00:45:29.489
That's nature. Jon.
You can't fight it.

537
00:45:31.739 --> 00:45:33.946
For me.
it was almost meditative.

538
00:45:33.947 --> 00:45:36.361
doing all the household work
with little Jon.

539
00:45:36.362 --> 00:45:38.779
-He was such a happy baby.
-Oh. Mum!

540
00:45:38.780 --> 00:45:41.612
Well. you were...
my little sunshine.

541
00:45:42.737 --> 00:45:44.779
Kuura doesn't really smile.

542
00:45:44.780 --> 00:45:46.904
Well. of course.
every baby is different.

543
00:45:46.905 --> 00:45:49.404
but we raise them with our love.

544
00:45:49.405 --> 00:45:52.571
It really is the greatest
happiness in the world

545
00:45:52.572 --> 00:45:54.361
to be a mother.

546
00:45:54.362 --> 00:45:55.654
Don't you think?

547
00:46:00.447 --> 00:46:02.696
It wasn't even hot!

548
00:46:02.697 --> 00:46:04.197
What did you do?

549
00:46:12.195 --> 00:46:15.153
What the hell did you do?

550
00:46:15.239 --> 00:46:16.988
There is no fire.

551
00:46:16.989 --> 00:46:18.819
It wasn't even near
the fireplace.

552
00:46:18.820 --> 00:46:21.864
Just for once. can you just
think about what you're doing?!

553
00:46:25.405 --> 00:46:28.695
It's just... cold.

554
00:46:30.195 --> 00:46:31.863
It's cold iron.

555
00:46:58.405 --> 00:47:00.489
I know what you are.

556
00:47:34.947 --> 00:47:35.947
Drink.

557
00:48:55.072 --> 00:48:56.655
Hey. babe!

558
00:49:16.945 --> 00:49:18.488
Us.

559
00:49:18.489 --> 00:49:20.195
All three.

560
00:49:27.489 --> 00:49:29.195
Oh.

561
00:49:33.612 --> 00:49:35.572
How's the formula going down?

562
00:49:37.030 --> 00:49:38.447
Oh...

563
00:49:39.780 --> 00:49:43.486
You know. he actually slurps up
as much as he can get.

564
00:49:43.487 --> 00:49:45.361
-Wow.
-Yeah.

565
00:49:45.362 --> 00:49:47.029
Great.

566
00:49:47.030 --> 00:49:49.486
Maybe now I can feed him. too.

567
00:49:49.487 --> 00:49:51.861
So it doesn't just fall on you.

568
00:49:51.862 --> 00:49:54.486
Yeah.

569
00:49:54.487 --> 00:49:58.947
I think it's better I feed him.
At least for now.

570
00:50:00.572 --> 00:50:01.780
Okay.

571
00:50:04.072 --> 00:50:05.361
How was work?

572
00:50:05.362 --> 00:50:08.070
Yeah. Good. Just...

573
00:50:09.364 --> 00:50:10.652
so Finnish.

574
00:50:14.195 --> 00:50:15.739
What?

575
00:50:20.195 --> 00:50:24.154
When is the last time
I asked you anything like...

576
00:50:24.155 --> 00:50:25.569
"Did you have a good day?"

577
00:50:25.570 --> 00:50:27.319
This is terrible.

578
00:50:27.320 --> 00:50:30.113
Hmm. Wow.

579
00:50:30.114 --> 00:50:32.486
The first year is the worst.

580
00:50:32.487 --> 00:50:33.821
Yeah.

581
00:50:33.822 --> 00:50:36.112
Divorce rates off the scale.

582
00:50:41.362 --> 00:50:45.029
You haven't thought about
anything like that. have you?

583
00:50:45.030 --> 00:50:47.071
-What? Divorce?
-Yeah.

584
00:50:47.072 --> 00:50:49.487
No. Of course not.

585
00:50:51.362 --> 00:50:54.862
I tell you everything.
You tell me everything. yeah?

586
00:50:56.655 --> 00:50:57.987
Yeah.

587
00:51:01.280 --> 00:51:02.946
You remember how we were saying

588
00:51:02.947 --> 00:51:05.779
we were gonna start
on another one about now?

589
00:51:05.780 --> 00:51:07.946
Can you imagine
being pregnant now?

590
00:51:07.947 --> 00:51:09.739
Yeah.

591
00:51:12.028 --> 00:51:13.364
I'm joking.

592
00:51:16.239 --> 00:51:17.614
Yeah.

593
00:51:20.320 --> 00:51:23.069
It'll come...

594
00:51:23.070 --> 00:51:25.194
when it's time.

595
00:51:25.195 --> 00:51:26.820
Yeah. Yeah.

596
00:51:32.072 --> 00:51:34.404
By the way.
when's your appointment?

597
00:51:34.405 --> 00:51:36.404
-Appointment?
-Yeah. The referral.

598
00:51:36.405 --> 00:51:38.822
The children's
health-clinic thing.

599
00:51:42.322 --> 00:51:44.155
You didn't book it.

600
00:51:47.322 --> 00:51:52.361
I feel so bad when you tell
everyone I've got problems.

601
00:51:52.362 --> 00:51:53.654
Yeah. we do have problems.

602
00:51:53.655 --> 00:51:55.236
I don't want you
to speak for me.

603
00:51:55.237 --> 00:51:56.611
That was the whole point.

604
00:51:56.612 --> 00:51:57.821
that you could
speak for yourself.

605
00:51:57.822 --> 00:51:59.696
I'm telling you now.

606
00:51:59.697 --> 00:52:02.277
You could trust me at least
a bit and give me some space.

607
00:52:02.278 --> 00:52:03.696
That's what
I've been trying to do!

608
00:52:03.697 --> 00:52:07.280
Don't correct me!
Stop interfering!

609
00:52:10.320 --> 00:52:12.445
Space. Okay.

610
00:52:18.364 --> 00:52:20.155
Jon.

611
00:52:32.697 --> 00:52:35.655
Jon! Jon!

612
00:54:10.739 --> 00:54:11.902
Hah!

613
00:54:21.030 --> 00:54:22.614
MUM

614
00:54:33.030 --> 00:54:35.237
Hi! Where are you?

615
00:54:35.862 --> 00:54:37.696
-It's Kuura.
-What?

616
00:54:37.697 --> 00:54:40.321
-What's that noise?
-It's Kuura!

617
00:54:40.322 --> 00:54:42.486
Who else has he mauled already?

618
00:54:44.780 --> 00:54:46.486
Hey. is everything alright?

619
00:54:48.530 --> 00:54:50.736
-You never ask that.
-Well. I'm asking now.

620
00:54:50.737 --> 00:54:51.737
Yes.

621
00:54:52.612 --> 00:54:53.779
Or I'm just...

622
00:54:56.947 --> 00:54:59.361
Sometimes I think

623
00:54:59.362 --> 00:55:02.486
I'm going to kill that child
if it doesn't get me first.

624
00:55:02.487 --> 00:55:06.572
You know. I thought exactly
the same when you were little.

625
00:55:07.737 --> 00:55:08.653
You did?

626
00:55:08.739 --> 00:55:15.152
Yes. this one time
I was so tired of your screaming

627
00:55:15.153 --> 00:55:18.864
that I left you outside a shop
and drove away.

628
00:55:19.905 --> 00:55:23.694
Well. I drove back
and took you with me.

629
00:55:23.695 --> 00:55:28.945
But at the time I had the
feeling you were sucking me dry.

630
00:55:30.695 --> 00:55:32.611
You were just a terrible child.

631
00:55:32.612 --> 00:55:36.361
They always say
that the wonderful moments

632
00:55:36.362 --> 00:55:39.486
make up for the hard ones
many times over.

633
00:55:39.487 --> 00:55:41.736
But I wouldn't be so sure.

634
00:55:41.737 --> 00:55:44.696
Go away! Go away!

635
00:55:45.697 --> 00:55:47.611
Saga. what's happening?

636
00:57:18.445 --> 00:57:19.780
Saga!

637
00:57:25.864 --> 00:57:27.280
Saga!

638
00:57:57.112 --> 00:57:58.696
Where have you been?

639
00:57:58.697 --> 00:58:01.363
Where have you been?

640
00:58:01.364 --> 00:58:03.653
Where's Kuura's clothes?!
He'll freeze to death!

641
00:58:05.530 --> 00:58:06.987
Get inside.

642
00:58:14.989 --> 00:58:16.739
Looking for this?

643
00:58:20.820 --> 00:58:23.820
Just please tell me
you have an explanation.

644
00:58:25.114 --> 00:58:27.738
-It won't drink milk.
-Neither do I!

645
00:58:27.739 --> 00:58:30.989
W-What are you gonna do.
start putting blood in my tea?!

646
00:58:33.447 --> 00:58:36.486
No. You are not giving another
drop of blood to our son.

647
00:58:36.487 --> 00:58:37.861
It won't take anything else.

648
00:58:37.862 --> 00:58:40.154
-Saga. please.
-Give it to me.

649
00:58:40.155 --> 00:58:41.861
-Let go!
-Give it to me!

650
00:58:41.862 --> 00:58:43.236
Saga!

651
00:59:13.864 --> 00:59:16.569
I don't know
who you are anymore.

652
00:59:16.570 --> 00:59:19.738
If I don't give it blood.
it'll suck it out of me.

653
00:59:19.739 --> 00:59:21.738
It'll kill me.

654
00:59:21.739 --> 00:59:24.570
I don't know if I'm more afraid
for you or for Kuura.

655
00:59:25.905 --> 00:59:27.905
So what do you want to do?

656
00:59:29.820 --> 00:59:32.446
Pick a day.

657
00:59:32.447 --> 00:59:34.986
Go into town.

658
00:59:34.987 --> 00:59:37.737
Go... Go and see some friends.

659
00:59:39.155 --> 00:59:40.946
Get yourself better.

660
00:59:40.947 --> 00:59:42.987
While I take care of Kuura.

661
00:59:44.655 --> 00:59:46.530
I want you to see...

662
00:59:46.655 --> 00:59:50.362
you don't have to
destroy yourself... or us.

663
00:59:52.862 --> 00:59:54.947
I want you to be happy again.

664
00:59:56.987 --> 00:59:59.487
For us to be happy together.

665
01:00:05.655 --> 01:00:07.111
Me too.

666
01:01:29.320 --> 01:01:30.530
How are you?

667
01:01:32.072 --> 01:01:33.447
How's work?

668
01:01:37.530 --> 01:01:38.905
I've missed you.

669
01:01:49.155 --> 01:01:51.530
Hey. there's the Mum!

670
01:01:52.697 --> 01:01:56.112
She's enjoyed the nesting life
while we've slaved away!

671
01:01:59.697 --> 01:02:01.072
We want to see photos!

672
01:02:02.778 --> 01:02:05.655
I don't really have
too many good ones.

673
01:02:07.112 --> 01:02:09.153
I so remember that.
no time to snap away.

674
01:02:09.239 --> 01:02:11.614
All we have
are some terrible blurry pics.

675
01:02:12.195 --> 01:02:15.070
-I'll take the vegetarian menu.
-It's really. really good.

676
01:02:21.905 --> 01:02:23.819
So. how's work?

677
01:02:23.820 --> 01:02:25.238
No. no talk about work!

678
01:02:25.239 --> 01:02:27.238
Your life is much
more important!

679
01:02:27.239 --> 01:02:30.738
Show us at least one pic.
this is not an official event.

680
01:02:30.739 --> 01:02:33.529
I so remember that being
the best time of my life.

681
01:02:33.530 --> 01:02:34.530
Yeah!

682
01:02:35.072 --> 01:02:37.905
We just talked
about how nice you always were.

683
01:02:38.155 --> 01:02:41.196
-Thank you.
-But then I suddenly realised.

684
01:02:41.197 --> 01:02:45.654
None of us really knows you.
you know?

685
01:02:48.155 --> 01:02:49.737
Maybe it's the Boss Role.

686
01:02:55.030 --> 01:02:57.611
I've actually missed work a lot.

687
01:02:57.612 --> 01:03:01.113
Hey. been there.
The sense of duty knocking.

688
01:03:01.114 --> 01:03:04.696
Your stand-in guy has
actually been quite good.

689
01:03:43.947 --> 01:03:45.072
Are you allergic?

690
01:03:45.612 --> 01:03:48.486
-Did you have the shrimp?
-No. the vegetarian menu.

691
01:03:48.487 --> 01:03:49.655
-Nuts?
-I've got to go.

692
01:03:53.905 --> 01:03:54.905
Hey!

693
01:04:13.114 --> 01:04:16.363
Hey.

694
01:04:16.364 --> 01:04:20.530
Hey. Alright. Yeah. Okay.

695
01:04:42.405 --> 01:04:45.071
What happened?

696
01:04:45.072 --> 01:04:47.486
Are you okay? Talk to me.

697
01:06:03.278 --> 01:06:07.362
Anyway. just trying
to support Saga.

698
01:06:08.489 --> 01:06:10.739
She's still having
a pretty rough time.

699
01:06:11.653 --> 01:06:15.320
What about you?
Like. deep down.

700
01:06:17.530 --> 01:06:19.613
Was just...

701
01:06:19.614 --> 01:06:22.779
I was so looking forward
to being a family.

702
01:06:22.780 --> 01:06:24.114
Ohh.

703
01:06:25.780 --> 01:06:27.529
Being a dad.

704
01:06:27.530 --> 01:06:29.320
You're doing great.

705
01:06:35.822 --> 01:06:37.987
I'm always away.

706
01:06:39.072 --> 01:06:42.111
I don't know
what's going on here.

707
01:06:42.112 --> 01:06:44.947
I think Saga is just exhausted.

708
01:06:49.487 --> 01:06:51.737
I think it's something
more than that.

709
01:06:56.030 --> 01:06:57.362
Nice.

710
01:06:58.530 --> 01:07:01.697
Juice for madam.

711
01:07:03.237 --> 01:07:04.654
Thanks...

712
01:07:10.570 --> 01:07:12.028
Um...

713
01:07:12.528 --> 01:07:15.528
Anna. go and play
with your cousin Kuura.

714
01:07:15.614 --> 01:07:16.780
No!

715
01:07:20.155 --> 01:07:21.488
It's not safe.

716
01:07:21.489 --> 01:07:23.280
Shut the fuck up!

717
01:07:25.945 --> 01:07:28.069
I'm gonna go and. uh...

718
01:07:28.070 --> 01:07:29.529
shovel some snow.

719
01:07:31.489 --> 01:07:32.779
Mother.

720
01:07:32.780 --> 01:07:33.862
It's all right.

721
01:07:37.362 --> 01:07:38.362
Hi.

722
01:07:45.072 --> 01:07:46.029
It's just awful.

723
01:07:46.030 --> 01:07:48.405
we still haven't got those boxes
unpacked.

724
01:07:59.197 --> 01:08:04.822
I so hoped for a lovely and nice
little girl like Anna.

725
01:08:08.239 --> 01:08:09.819
But instead...

726
01:08:13.364 --> 01:08:14.989
I got that monster.

727
01:08:21.320 --> 01:08:24.361
Studies say that if you don't
show empathy to your child

728
01:08:24.362 --> 01:08:26.904
during the first three years.
he may never learn it.

729
01:08:28.362 --> 01:08:30.653
I've given that thing
absolutely everything.

730
01:08:30.654 --> 01:08:31.654
Right.

731
01:08:32.197 --> 01:08:34.237
It just takes and takes and
takes.

732
01:08:34.822 --> 01:08:37.072
Soon there'll be nothing left of
me.

733
01:08:38.697 --> 01:08:40.778
But I can't be without it.

734
01:08:40.779 --> 01:08:42.822
And I don't see the sense in
that.

735
01:08:44.487 --> 01:08:46.529
And where's the happiness?

736
01:08:47.404 --> 01:08:49.821
Things don't always go as
planned.

737
01:08:49.822 --> 01:08:53.947
I just wanted our kids to have
what we had.

738
01:08:54.862 --> 01:08:57.404
You're really living in a
reality all your own.

739
01:08:58.072 --> 01:09:01.072
You think I really had fun
playing with you as a child?

740
01:09:02.279 --> 01:09:03.612
Everything had to be

741
01:09:03.613 --> 01:09:06.778
on your terms. and no matter
how shitty you acted

742
01:09:06.779 --> 01:09:09.111
you were the one who needed to
be understood.

743
01:09:09.112 --> 01:09:10.320
And it's still the same.

744
01:09:11.404 --> 01:09:14.654
Mum called me to ask how you and
Kuura are doing.

745
01:09:16.070 --> 01:09:17.779
But nothing about me or Anna.

746
01:09:20.487 --> 01:09:22.654
Because we
must be doing really great.

747
01:09:23.737 --> 01:09:25.111
You're still making

748
01:09:25.112 --> 01:09:28.319
such a big deal of your
problems and emotions

749
01:09:28.320 --> 01:09:30.861
that there's no room for the
rest of us.

750
01:09:30.862 --> 01:09:33.612
Now you've moved on to
smothering your own child!

751
01:09:34.987 --> 01:09:36.779
There's nothing wrong with
Kuura!

752
01:09:37.822 --> 01:09:41.447
It's you who's making your
family life unbearable!

753
01:09:42.822 --> 01:09:44.196
No one else!

754
01:09:49.822 --> 01:09:51.236
Anna!

755
01:09:51.237 --> 01:09:52.486
Hey! Hey!

756
01:09:53.779 --> 01:09:56.571
Darling.
it's alright! Show me.

757
01:09:57.737 --> 01:09:59.028
Let me see!

758
01:09:59.029 --> 01:10:00.528
Saga. just leave it!

759
01:10:00.529 --> 01:10:02.528
It's alright. we'll take you to
a hospital.

760
01:10:02.529 --> 01:10:03.737
Taru?

761
01:10:03.738 --> 01:10:05.197
You're the monster!

762
01:11:57.904 --> 01:11:59.903
Ahhh!

763
01:11:59.904 --> 01:12:01.822
Ah!

764
01:12:11.237 --> 01:12:13.111
Wah. wah. wah.

765
01:12:13.112 --> 01:12:15.569
Ah. ah.

766
01:12:15.570 --> 01:12:17.653
Ah!

767
01:12:24.112 --> 01:12:25.736
Wah. wah.

768
01:12:27.570 --> 01:12:30.237
Whee!

769
01:14:31.737 --> 01:14:34.653
That wasn't so bad. was it?

770
01:14:34.654 --> 01:14:37.736
Look at him. all dressed up.

771
01:14:37.737 --> 01:14:42.571
Now we can have a nice old
proper family dinner.

772
01:14:42.572 --> 01:14:44.946
Let's get you in here.

773
01:14:44.947 --> 01:14:46.903
Let me just get your leg
through there.

774
01:14:53.154 --> 01:14:55.447
Have you spoken to Taru yet?

775
01:14:56.904 --> 01:14:58.736
Anna's doing better.

776
01:14:58.737 --> 01:15:01.446
If you're interested. that is.

777
01:15:01.447 --> 01:15:04.197
But her finger
is gonna remain a stump.

778
01:15:07.113 --> 01:15:09.654
What do you want from me?

779
01:15:13.445 --> 01:15:17.278
Kuura. let's teach you
some table manners.

780
01:15:17.279 --> 01:15:19.361
Okay?

781
01:15:20.654 --> 01:15:23.528
Ah. Kuura.

782
01:15:23.529 --> 01:15:25.903
Say "please."

783
01:15:25.904 --> 01:15:28.236
Here comes the airplane.

784
01:15:33.654 --> 01:15:37.361
Starting from now...

785
01:15:37.362 --> 01:15:39.572
we're gonna
raise this child right.

786
01:15:41.572 --> 01:15:44.236
So I'm setting some limits.

787
01:15:44.237 --> 01:15:48.028
Human limits.

788
01:15:48.029 --> 01:15:49.861
Right.

789
01:15:49.862 --> 01:15:52.071
Here comes the airplane.

790
01:16:01.572 --> 01:16:04.446
It's as much my fault
as it is yours.

791
01:16:07.072 --> 01:16:09.069
Ohh.

792
01:16:17.862 --> 01:16:20.070
Okay.

793
01:16:21.654 --> 01:16:23.153
Okay.

794
01:16:23.154 --> 01:16:25.653
Here comes...

795
01:16:25.654 --> 01:16:27.737
the airplane.

796
01:16:29.070 --> 01:16:32.903
Wheeeeee.

797
01:16:36.697 --> 01:16:38.528
The metal hurts him!

798
01:16:38.529 --> 01:16:41.154
Oh. will you just give
your fucking fantasies a rest?!

799
01:16:47.822 --> 01:16:50.361
Sorry. Kuura.

800
01:16:50.362 --> 01:16:53.446
Mommy and Daddy are
just having a little argument.

801
01:16:53.447 --> 01:16:55.447
It's all gonna be fine.

802
01:16:57.362 --> 01:16:58.861
Here comes the airplane.

803
01:17:01.029 --> 01:17:03.403
This child...

804
01:17:03.404 --> 01:17:05.821
can't be raised.

805
01:17:05.822 --> 01:17:07.321
Don't say that.

806
01:17:07.322 --> 01:17:09.486
There's nothing
you can do about it.

807
01:17:09.487 --> 01:17:11.569
You're wrong.
I'll prove you wrong.

808
01:17:11.570 --> 01:17:12.903
Let it eat.

809
01:17:12.904 --> 01:17:14.069
"Him"!

810
01:17:14.070 --> 01:17:15.444
I'm not just gonna stand here

811
01:17:15.445 --> 01:17:16.819
and watch you turn him
into a monster.

812
01:17:16.820 --> 01:17:20.861
Leave it alooooone!

813
01:17:33.197 --> 01:17:35.447
It's asleep.

814
01:17:43.572 --> 01:17:45.779
I should apologize.

815
01:17:47.404 --> 01:17:49.529
Okay.

816
01:17:52.947 --> 01:17:54.947
I guess...

817
01:17:57.279 --> 01:17:59.447
for many things.

818
01:18:01.112 --> 01:18:03.072
Thank you.

819
01:18:05.113 --> 01:18:06.696
For what?

820
01:18:06.697 --> 01:18:09.779
For showing me
who you really are.

821
01:18:15.362 --> 01:18:18.237
It's just. it's been too hard.

822
01:18:20.237 --> 01:18:21.944
-Kuura is...
-You're right.

823
01:18:21.945 --> 01:18:24.028
But not Kuura.

824
01:18:24.029 --> 01:18:25.778
You.

825
01:18:25.779 --> 01:18:28.111
What?

826
01:18:28.112 --> 01:18:30.320
I always wanted a big family.

827
01:18:32.072 --> 01:18:34.278
And then we met.

828
01:18:34.279 --> 01:18:37.903
And I could see
our entire future.

829
01:18:37.904 --> 01:18:39.403
Me too.

830
01:18:39.404 --> 01:18:41.529
But you killed it.

831
01:18:45.487 --> 01:18:50.278
And now it's like
I can't feel anything anymore.

832
01:18:50.279 --> 01:18:55.196
It's like this impossibly heavy
weight is pushing me down.

833
01:18:55.197 --> 01:18:58.611
Just because you feel bad
for being away so much.

834
01:18:58.612 --> 01:19:01.112
You should never
have been a mother.

835
01:19:03.238 --> 01:19:06.571
You hate our child.

836
01:19:06.572 --> 01:19:10.112
You've turned him
completely dysfunctional.

837
01:19:12.487 --> 01:19:14.528
I don't think you know
how to love.

838
01:19:14.529 --> 01:19:17.944
I don't think you can love
anyone.

839
01:19:17.945 --> 01:19:20.569
I don't need to listen to this.

840
01:19:20.570 --> 01:19:22.569
You never listen to anyone.

841
01:19:22.570 --> 01:19:25.486
You're so utterly.
blindingly selfish.

842
01:19:25.487 --> 01:19:26.861
Taru was right.

843
01:19:26.862 --> 01:19:29.028
You're the monster.

844
01:19:29.029 --> 01:19:31.653
And I'm taking Kuura away
from you.

845
01:19:31.654 --> 01:19:33.403
What?

846
01:19:33.404 --> 01:19:35.571
He still has a chance to be
a perfectly normal boy.

847
01:19:35.572 --> 01:19:37.153
He just needs professional help.

848
01:19:37.154 --> 01:19:38.946
So do you.

849
01:19:38.947 --> 01:19:41.486
You're not taking him.

850
01:19:41.487 --> 01:19:43.321
I'm saving our child.

851
01:19:43.322 --> 01:19:44.696
I've already spoken
to my parents.

852
01:19:44.697 --> 01:19:46.446
It's done.

853
01:19:46.447 --> 01:19:48.653
-Let go.
-And I'm gonna get full custody.

854
01:19:48.654 --> 01:19:50.153
Let go!

855
01:19:50.154 --> 01:19:52.028
You're hurting him!

856
01:19:52.029 --> 01:19:53.196
You're hurting him!

857
01:19:53.197 --> 01:19:54.946
You're hurting him!
